.TH LUMART 1 "October 2026" "Lumart 2.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lumart, luma \- High-Fidelity Terminal Visual Suite (Mary Apex, Trumble Orelx, Luris Mono, Spectra Weep)

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lumart
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIIMAGE_PATH_OR_URL\fR]
.br
.B lumart
.B diff
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIIMAGE_A\fR \fIIMAGE_B\fR
.br
.B luma
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIIMAGE_PATH_OR_URL\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBlumart\fR is an industrial-grade terminal image and video renderer designed for high-definition visual fidelity in modern terminal emulators. Powered by C++17 OpenMP SIMD routines and Python OpenCV acceleration, Lumart projects raster graphics, vector animations, manga screentones, and real-time webcam video feeds directly into standard ANSI/Unicode text viewports.

Lumart routes inputs across four flagship rendering engines:
.TP
.B Mary Apex 3.5
Photorealistic vector TrueColor engine using the \fBOklab perceptual color space\fR, discrete 31-partition combinatorial optimization per sextant cell, and SIMD-accelerated C++17.
.TP
.B Trumble Orelx 2.2
Capcom CPS-2 retro-arcade cel-shading engine featuring \fB1-to-1 subpixel Canny edge detection\fR, Retinex multi-scale contrast, and vibrant comic punch.
.TP
.B Luris Mono 2.6
Japanese manga screentone and line-art engine utilizing \fB8x8 Bayer halftone matrices\fR, adaptive Difference-of-Gaussians (DoG) edge filters, and transparent background PNG sticker generation.
.TP
.B Spectra Weep 1.4
Hardware-accelerated real-time video and webcam streaming engine operating at 30\(en60 FPS with live terminal shader matrix filters.

.SH OPTIONS

.SS "Engine Selection"
.TP
\fB\-E\fR, \fB\-\-engine\fR \fIENGINE\fR
Explicitly select the rendering engine. Supported values: \fBmary\fR, \fBtrumble\fR, \fBluris\fR, \fBspectra\fR, \fBcolor\fR, \fBmono\fR, \fBbw\fR, \fBmanga\fR, \fBsketch\fR. By default, Lumart automatically routes based on options and content.

.SS "Subpixel Textures & Halftones"
.TP
\fB\-S\fR, \fB\-\-sextants\fR
Render using Unicode 2\(mu3 Sextant characters (U+1FB00\(enU+1FB3B). Default for Mary Apex. Yields 6 subpixels per cell with independent foreground and background colors.
.TP
\fB\-B\fR, \fB\-\-braille\fR
Render using Unicode 2\(mu4 Braille patterns (U+2800\(enU+28FF). Yields 8 subpixels per character cell, ideal for fine stippling and detailed sketches.
.TP
\fB\-Q\fR, \fB\-\-quadrants\fR
Render using Unicode 2\(mu2 Quadrant block characters (4 subpixels per cell).
.TP
\fB\-\-blocks\fR
Render using optimized half-block characters (\(ua / \(da) with independent foreground and background colors.
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-manga\fR
Activate Manga Screentone 2.0 mode (Bayer 8\(mu8 matrix dithering combined with adaptive DoG vector ink outlines).
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-sketch\fR
Activate clean line sketch mode without screentone dithering.

.SS "Viewport, Framing & Zoom"
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-width\fR \fICOLUMNS\fR
Set explicit output width in terminal character columns. Incompatible with \fB\-F\fR / \fB\-\-fit\fR.
.TP
\fB\-F\fR, \fB\-\-fit\fR
\fBAuto-fit to terminal viewport\fR: dynamically queries terminal rows and columns, calculating optimal bounding box without vertical scrolling. Incompatible with \fB\-w\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-crop\fR \fISPEC\fR
Frame and crop image: \fBcenter\fR, \fBsquare\fR (1:1), or specific coordinates \fBx,y,w,h\fR (e.g. \fI10%,10%,80%,80%\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-zoom\fR \fIFACTOR\fR
Digital zoom centered on subject using high-quality Lanczos resampling (e.g. \fB\-\-zoom 1.5\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-font\-ratio\fR \fIRATIO\fR
Calibrate terminal font width-to-height aspect ratio (default: \fB0.5\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-fastfetch\fR, \fB\-\-logo\fR
Auto-crop transparent and empty bounding margins for Fastfetch or Neofetch sidebars.

.SS "Color, Tone & Themes"
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-color\fR
Force TrueColor (24-bit RGB) ANSI rendering (default).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable color escape sequences and route to monochrome pipeline.
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\fR, \fB\-\-palette\fR \fITHEME\fR
Synchronize palette with popular terminal themes: \fBcatppuccin\fR, \fBdracula\fR, \fBnord\fR, \fBgruvbox\fR, \fBsynthwave\fR, \fBvaporwave\fR, \fBgameboy\fR, \fBsolarized\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-crt\fR, \fB\-\-scanlines\fR [\fIMODE\fR]
Simulate retro cathode ray tube monitors and phosphor displays (\fBcolor\fR, \fBgreen\fR P1 phosphor, \fBamber\fR P3 phosphor, \fBscanlines\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-matrix\fR
Render image using Katakana code ramp and phosphor green Matrix palette.
.TP
\fB\-\-matrix\-rain\fR
Animate falling digital Katakana Matrix rain resolving smoothly into the image.
.TP
\fB\-\-boost\fR, \fB\-\-vibrant\fR
Apply Retinex multi-scale contrast and saturation boost for arcade vibrancy.
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-invert\fR
Invert luminance values (useful for light terminal backgrounds).
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-dither\fR [\fIALGORITHM\fR]
Select error-diffusion algorithm: \fBatkinson\fR (default), \fBfloyd\fR, \fBbayer\fR, or \fBnone\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-swap\fR \fICOLOR1\fR \fICOLOR2\fR
Dynamically swap colors within 3D RGB Euclidean color space.

.SS "Background Removal & Stickers"
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-remove\-bg\fR
Intelligent AI background removal without quality loss. If invoked standalone (\fBlumart \-r img.png\fR), exports a full-resolution transparent PNG with zero quality degradation. If combined with engine flags (\fBlumart \-r \-E mary img.png\fR), removes the background first and renders the isolated subject in terminal ASCII.
.TP
\fB\-\-transparent\fR
Export manga renders as alpha-transparent PNG stickers (Luris Mono exclusive).

.SS "Interactive TUI, Gallery & Diff"
.TP
\fB\-I\fR, \fB\-\-interactive\fR, \fB\-\-tui\fR
Launch interactive live parameter tuning TUI directly inside the terminal. Real-time keys: \fB[+/-]\fR adjust width, \fB[M]\fR switch engine, \fB[T]\fR switch theme palette, \fB[C]\fR toggle CRT filter, \fB[D]\fR cycle dither, \fB[B]\fR toggle boost, \fB[S]\fR save, \fB[Enter]\fR print, \fB[Q]\fR quit.
.TP
\fB\-\-slideshow\fR [\fIPATHS...\fR]
Interactive terminal image gallery slideshow with controls (\fB[Space]\fR next, \fB[Arrows]\fR navigate, \fB[P]\fR pause, \fB[R]\fR random, \fB[Q]\fR quit).
.TP
\fB\-\-delay\fR \fISECONDS\fR
Slideshow interval duration (default: \fB3.0\fR).
.TP
\fBlumart diff\fR \fIIMG1\fR \fIIMG2\fR, \fB\-\-diff\fR \fIIMG2\fR
Visual side-by-side terminal image comparison with dual-pane layout and RMSE pixel color delta telemetry.

.SS "Export, Clipboard & UNIX Pipes"
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-O\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR, \fB\-\-save\fR \fIFILE\fR
Export render to graphical image (\fB.png\fR, \fB.jpg\fR), animated GIF (\fB.gif\fR), raw ANSI truecolor buffer (\fB.ans\fR, \fB.asc\fR for zero-delay MOTD), or plain text (\fB.txt\fR).
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-copy\fR
Copy rendered ANSI truecolor art directly to system clipboard via Wayland (\fIwl-copy\fR), X11 (\fIxclip\fR, \fIxsel\fR), or macOS (\fIpbcopy\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-copy\-plain\fR
Copy plain ASCII text stripped of ANSI escape codes to clipboard for Markdown or Discord codeblocks.
.TP
\fB\-\fR (STDIN)
Pipe binary image stream directly from UNIX standard input (\fIcat image.png | lumart \-\fR or \fIcurl \-s URL | lumart \-\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-paste\fR
Grab image data directly from system clipboard.
.TP
\fB\-\-loop\fR
Animation mode: caches frames in memory for smooth 60 FPS terminal playback, or compiles animated GIF when paired with \fB\-o file.gif\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-instant\fR, \fB\-\-no\-reveal\fR
Display render output immediately without progressive line scanning (default).
.TP
\fB\-\-reveal\fR
Enable progressive top-to-bottom scanline reveal animation.

.SS "System Utilities & Lifecycle"
.TP
\fB\-W\fR, \fB\-\-webcam\fR [\fICAMERA_INDEX\fR]
Launch real-time webcam terminal stream at 30\(en60 FPS (default index: 0).
.TP
\fB\-\-lang\fR \fICODE\fR
Set interface language (\fBen\fR, \fBes\fR, \fBpt\fR, \fBfr\fR, \fBru\fR, \fBja\fR, \fBde\fR, \fBko\fR).
.TP
\fB\-H\fR, \fB\-\-history\fR [\fIN\fR]
Display last N executed commands from persistent command history.
.TP
\fB\-R\fR, \fB\-\-replay\fR [\fIN\fR]
Re-run the N-th command from history (default: last command).
.TP
\fB\-\-clear\-history\fR
Wipe all command history from \fI~/.config/luma/history\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-install\-desktop\fR
Install desktop integration and file manager context menu entry ("Open with Lumart").
.TP
\fB\-\-completions\fR \fISHELL\fR
Generate shell tab-completion script for \fBbash\fR, \fBzsh\fR, or \fBfish\fR.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Display diagnostic card detailing hardware architecture, OS, Python version, C++ compiler, SIMD/OpenMP support, and engine health.
.TP
\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-update\fR, \fB\-\-check\-update\fR
Query GitHub API for available upstream updates.
.TP
\fB\-uu\fR, \fB\-\-upgrade\fR
Perform automated in-place upgrade to latest upstream release.
.TP
\fB\-dg\fR, \fB\-\-downgrade\fR [\fIVERSION\fR]
Rollback to previously installed version or specific release.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful completion.
.TP
.B 1
General runtime error (file not found, invalid URL, unreadable image).
.TP
.B 2
CLI argument validation error or mutually exclusive flag conflict (e.g. \fB\-\-fit\fR combined with \fB\-\-width\fR).

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/luma/history
Command execution history log.
.TP
.I ~/.config/luma/backup/
Backup archives for version rollback.
.TP
.I ~/.config/luma/config.json
User preferences (language, default flags).

.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Remove background cleanly with zero quality loss:
.RS
.B lumart \-r photo.jpg
.RE
.PP
Remove background and render isolated subject in Mary Apex TrueColor:
.RS
.B lumart \-r \-E mary photo.jpg \-w 80
.RE
.PP
Side-by-side terminal image diff comparison:
.RS
.B lumart diff before.png after.png \-w 100
.RE
.PP
Synchronize render with Dracula terminal palette:
.RS
.B lumart avatar.png \-\-theme dracula
.RE
.PP
Retro green phosphor CRT monitor simulation:
.RS
.B lumart logo.png \-\-crt green
.RE
.PP
Katakana Matrix code ramp:
.RS
.B lumart cyber.jpg \-\-matrix
.RE
.PP
Interactive Live TUI adjustment mode:
.RS
.B lumart \-I image.png
.RE
.PP
Interactive terminal slideshow of a directory:
.RS
.B lumart \-\-slideshow wallpapers/ \-\-delay 4.0
.RE
.PP
Pipe image from STDIN and copy ANSI truecolor render to clipboard:
.RS
.B cat banner.png | lumart \- \-w 60 \-C
.RE
.PP
Export raw ANSI banner for instant zero-delay MOTD in .bashrc:
.RS
.B lumart logo.png \-o ~/.config/motd.ans
.RE

